        "text": "Installing VS Code\nGetting VS Code onto our Pi is even easier. VS Code is included in the official repositories for Raspberry\nPi OS, so we don\u2019t need to manually download files or set up alternative repositories \u2013 we can just\nopen the terminal and type the following:\nsudo apt-get update\nsudo apt install code\nOnce we\u2019ve done this, after a few minutes, VS Code will appear on our machine alongside a lot of chatter:\nFigure 15.4 \u2013 Installing and starting VS Code on the Raspberry Pi\nWe can either type code in the terminal, or we can find it in the Programming subsection of the\napplications menu by clicking on the raspberry icon in the top-left corner.\nNow, let\u2019s look at the most common way I use the Raspberry Pi: remotely.",
